BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 782 Td (Lexical analysis is the first compiler phase. It converts raw source characters into meaningful) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 769 Td (tokens while tracking line/column information and stripping comments/whitespace.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 747 Td (Q2: What is parsing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 731 Td (Parsing \(syntax analysis\) takes the token stream from the lexer and verifies whether it conforms to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 718 Td (the formal BNF grammar, constructing an Abstract Syntax Tree \(AST\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 696 Td (Q3: Why recursive descent parsing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 680 Td (Recursive descent parsing is a top-down technique where each non-terminal grammar rule is written) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 667 Td (as a clean, deterministic Python function. It requires zero external tools.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 645 Td (Q4: What is an AST?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 629 Td (An Abstract Syntax Tree \(AST\) is a hierarchical tree representation of source code logic, omitting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 616 Td (syntactic noise like semicolons and parentheses.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 594 Td (Q5: What is semantic analysis?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 578 Td (Semantic analysis checks static rules that context-free grammars cannot capture, such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 565 Td (declaration before use, block scope visibility, and type consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 543 Td (Q6: What is a symbol table?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 527 Td (A symbol table is a data structure storing identifier metadata \(name, type, scope level,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 514 Td (declaration location\) during compilation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 492 Td (Q7: What is lexical scope?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 476 Td (Lexical scope means variable visibility is determined by physical position in block structures \({) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 463 Td (... }\). Child blocks access parent variables, but not vice-versa.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 441 Td (Q8: What is variable shadowing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 425 Td (Variable shadowing occurs when an inner block declares a variable with the same name as an outer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 412 Td (variable, temporarily hiding the outer declaration.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 390 Td (Q9: What is Three-Address Code \(TAC\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 374 Td (TAC is an intermediate representation where each quadruple has at most 3 operands, breaking complex) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 361 Td (logic into flat, register-like hardware steps.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 339 Td (Q10: Why use temporary variables in TAC?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 323 Td (Temporary variables \(t1, t2, ...\) break down nested AST expressions into linear step-by-step) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 310 Td (instructions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 288 Td (Q11: What is constant folding?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 272 Td (Constant folding evaluates constant expressions \(e.g. 2 + 3 * 4 -> 14\) at compile time to save) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 259 Td (runtime computation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 237 Td (Q12: What is dead code elimination?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 221 Td (Dead code elimination removes unreachable instructions \(e.g. quadruples following an unconditional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 208 Td (GOTO jump\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 186 Td (Q13: Why interpret TAC instead of AST directly?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 170 Td (Interpreting TAC proves that intermediate code generation works correctly and demonstrates a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 157 Td (complete 5-phase compiler pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 135 Td (Q14: Difference between syntax and semantic errors?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 119 Td (Syntax errors violate grammar rules \(e.g. missing semicolon\). Semantic errors violate static logic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 106 Td (rules \(e.g. using an undeclared variable\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 84 Td (Q15: Difference between compile-time and runtime errors?) Tj ET
