BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 782 Td (Compile-time errors \(lexical, syntax, semantic\) are caught before execution. Runtime errors \(e.g.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 769 Td (division by zero\) occur during VM execution.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 747 Td (Q16: How are while loops represented in TAC?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 731 Td (Using two labels and jumps: a start label L1, condition evaluation, IF_FALSE GOTO L2, body) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 718 Td (quadruples, GOTO L1, and end label L2.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 696 Td (Q17: How is if/else represented in TAC?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 680 Td (Condition evaluation, IF_FALSE GOTO L1 \(else\), then-branch quadruples, GOTO L2 \(end\), label L1,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 667 Td (else-branch quadruples, label L2.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 645 Td (Q18: How is division by zero handled?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 629 Td (Skipped during compile-time constant folding to avoid compiler crashes; caught during VM execution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 616 Td (by raising a clean RuntimeError.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 594 Td (Q19: How is operator precedence implemented?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 578 Td (Through grammar method hierarchy: comparison -> addExpr \(+/-\) -> term \(*//\) -> factor, ensuring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 565 Td (higher precedence operators bind deeper in AST.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.2 rg 40 543 Td (Q20: What are the main limitations of Sudarshan?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 527 Td (Sudarshan supports only integer variables and single-file programs without functions, arrays,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.1 0.1 0.1 rg 40 514 Td (floats, or target assembly code generation.) Tj ET
endstream
